<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Emirate of Liptako</h1><p class="st-meta">1810 CE – 1897 CE (approx.) · capital Dori</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Fulbe emirate in northern Burkina Faso centred on Dori, created by jihad in 1810 and the westernmost outpost of the Sokoto Caliphate.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulbe</a> herders had settled in Liptako under the rule of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gurma-people">Gurma</a> chiefs. Around 1810, inspired by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihad</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usman-dan-fodio">Usman dan Fodio</a>, the Fulbe rose under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahima-saydu">Brahima Saydu</a>, defeated the Gurma and founded an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dori">Dori</a>. Its rulers accepted the authority of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gwandu-emirate">Gwandu Emirate</a>, which supervised the western emirates of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Liptako was a pastoral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahel">Sahel</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulbe</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> owners ruled over farming communities and slaves. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> governed with Muslim scholars and lineage heads, and were often weakened by succession disputes. The emirate fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gurma-people">Gurma</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuareg">Tuareg</a> neighbours for grazing land and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/well">wells</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heinrich-barth">Heinrich Barth</a> passed through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dori">Dori</a> in 1853 and described the town.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>French columns reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dori">Dori</a> in the 1890s, and Liptako came under French rule in 1897. It became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-sudan">French Sudan</a> and later of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-upper-volta">French Upper Volta</a>, and Dori remains the main town of the region.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 1810 CE – 1897 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:95.72%;width:1.73%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1810 CE – 1897 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dori</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Brahima Saydu</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Fulfulde</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/burkina-faso">Burkina Faso</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Liptako</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1854&amp;focus=emirate-of-liptako" aria-label="Emirate of Liptako on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4679 1655 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Emirate of Liptako lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4999 1911L5144 1947M4999 1911L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5144 1947h0M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4999 1911h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4999 1911h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Dori. <a href="/atlas?year=1854&amp;focus=emirate-of-liptako">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

